� Real-Time Trading Analytics Dashboard
 A professional, full-featured Streamlit web app for real-time financial market analysis — built with Python,
 MetaTrader 5, SQLite, and Plotly. This project demonstrates strong foundations in data engineering,
 visualization, and technical analysis automation.
 🚀 Features
 • 
• 
• 
• 
• 
• 
Real-time data fetch from MetaTrader5 API
 Symbol-level SQLite database for OHLCV data storage
 Automated indicator pipeline (RSI, MACD, ATR, ADX, Triple-EMA)
 Price Action analysis using ATR-adaptive swing detection and channel recognition
 Interactive visualization with Plotly (multi-tab dashboard)
 Streamlit-based UI for easy exploration and analysis
 🧱 Project Architecture
 MetaTrader5  →  Data Fetcher  →  SQLite DB  →  Indicator Manager  →  Streamlit 
Visualization
 Key Modules
 • 
• 
• 
• 
• 
mt5_connector/ → Connection and data fetching from MT5
 database/ → SQLite operations (save, update, retrieve)
 analysis/ → Indicator calculations and price action logic
 visualization/ → Plotly chart creation
 app.py → Streamlit front-end entry point
 🧩 How to Run Locally
 1
 ️
 ⃣ Clone the Repository
 git clone https://github.com/<your-username>/stream-master.git
 cd stream-master
 1
2
 ️
 ⃣ Create Virtual Environment
 python-m venv .venv
 source .venv/bin/activate # or .venv\Scripts\activate on Windows
 3
 ️
 ⃣ Install Requirements
 pip install-r requirements.txt
 4
 ️
 ⃣ Setup Environment Variables
 Create a file named 
.env in the project root with: 
MT5_LOGIN=your_login
 MT5_PASSWORD=your_password
 MT5_SERVER=your_server
 MT5_PATH=your_mt5_path
 (Use 
.env.example as a reference.)
 5
 ️
 ⃣ Run the App
 streamlit run app.py
 🧠 Demo Mode (No MT5 Required)
 If you don’t have access to MetaTrader5, use a sample CSV dataset instead: 
python scripts/create_sample_data.py
 streamlit run app.py----demo
 This will load example data (e.g., BTCUSD-H1.csv) and let you explore the interface fully.
